message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "A U.S. county-year panel of labor demand and skill specialization, relatedness, and complexity, by employer entity type, 2010-2024"
abstract: >-
  A publicly available county-year panel of U.S. labor and skill demand,
  derived from 433.6 million Lightcast (formerly Burning Glass) job postings
  spanning 2010-2024. The panel covers 3,194 counties across 15 years
  (47,891 county-year observations) and reports 201 variables organized into
  eleven groups: a 37-variable core set describing the volume, employer-entity
  composition, work mode and internships, skill content, specialization,
  complexity, relatedness, and dynamics of local labor demand, plus 164
  additional variables in the entity-decomposed extension covering
  entity-type specialization breadth, employer-pair skill-similarity, and
  per-employer-type dynamics for sectoral and spillover research.
